,"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Systems"}," that normally do not have an open firing arc when surrounded by the cargo ring.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Though Core Ships are tough, they can be brought down more easily than when attached to the cargo ring. Slow and lacking maneuverability, Core Ships are not the ideal landing craft; they are typically deployed to a planet only when the ship's operators believe that a long-term occupation is called for. Core Ships serve as mobile ground fortresses, carrying within them a large number of Droid Troops that can be deployed quickly. For more rapid (or more temporary) invasions, the Trade Federation continues to use normal landing craft and troop carriers, since a Core Ship on the ground is far more vulnerable than one in space.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Lucrehulk"]},"-Class Core Ship Statistics (CL 17)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal (Cruiser) ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," -2; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 13 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 13), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 52; +13 Armor, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicular Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicular_Combat","referenceId":"r